                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "DULL AS DISHWATER\r\n\r\nI normally have a broad spectrum with a forgiving bend for RPG Maker games, but this one is just so unbearably repetitive that I can't finish it.\r\n\r\nIt starts off innocently enough with playing through four (very brief) chapters for each party member, which you can easily go through in about an hour. Especially if you unequip the level 99 Lightbringer who selects the chapters then equip his random diamond stuff on each person and unequip them before finishing their level.\r\n\r\nThen the \"randomizer' comes in.\r\n\r\nFour or five screens' worth of randomizers for each dungeon. Thankfully monsters are on screen and don't seem to respawn, but what good is that when there are 500 of them per dungeon?\r\n\r\nI got to a part with 4 \"outer world\" dungeons, and each was fully 4 randomized screens of monsters and treasure chests. With a weird boss monster at the end of each with gobs of HP and nothing else to recommend it.\r\n\r\nIn one word: Repetitive. Do not play this game unless you want to piss away about 4-8 hours of your life in a vastly unrewarding milquetoast RPG.",
